      "content": "The ionic radii of K<sup>+</sup>, Na<sup>+</sup>, Al<sup>3+</sup> and Mg<sup>2+</sup> are in the order:",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "Na<sup>+</sup> &lt; K<sup>+</sup> &lt; Mg<sup>2+</sup> &lt; Al<sup>3+</sup>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "Al<sup>3+</sup> &lt; Mg<sup>2+</sup> &lt; K<sup>+</sup> &lt; Na<sup>+</sup>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "Al<sup>3+</sup> &lt; Mg<sup>2+</sup> &lt; Na<sup>+</sup> &lt; K<sup>+</sup>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "K<sup>+</sup> &lt; Al<sup>3+</sup> &lt; Mg<sup>2+</sup> &lt; Na<sup>+</sup>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "C"
      ],
      "explanation": "Al<sup>3+</sup>, Mg<sup>2+</sup> and Na<sup>+</sup> are isoelectronic ionic species. For monoatomic ionic isoelectronic species as positive charge increases ionic size decreases.<br><br>The order of size of Na<sup>+</sup> &amp; K<sup>+</sup> is Na<sup>+</sup> &lt; K<sup>+</sup><br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Order of ionic radii is : Al<sup>3+</sup> &lt; Mg<sup>2+</sup> &lt; Na<sup>+</sup> &lt; K<sup>+</sup>"
